CONTEXT
We are building a small, production-ready “Customer Directory” service for a client.
They want a REST API that can run locally and in Kubernetes later.
The client is security-conscious (public sector style), wants good logging/metrics/tracing, and expects tests and documentation.
TECH STACK
- Language: TypeScript
- Runtime: Node.js (LTS)
- Framework: Fastify (preferred) OR Express if needed
- Observability: OpenTelemetry (traces + metrics), JSON structured logs
- Persistence: SQLite for local demo (file-based), using Prisma ORM
- Auth: API key header (x-api-key) for simplicity
- Dev tooling: ESLint + Prettier
- Packaging: Dockerfile + docker-compose
FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
1) API endpoints:
   - GET /health (returns ok + version)
   - GET /customers?search=&page=&pageSize=
   - GET /customers/:id
   - POST /customers
   - PUT /customers/:id
   - DELETE /customers/:id
2) Customer model:
   - id (uuid)
   - name (string, required)
   - email (string, unique, required)
   - phone (string, optional)
   - createdAt, updatedAt
3) Validation:
   - Proper request validation with helpful error messages
   - Email format validation
4) Pagination:
   - page defaults to 1, pageSize defaults to 20, max pageSize 100
5) Search:
   - case-insensitive search on name and email
NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS
